 '...'`.\n\n**What's wrong**\n- **The function call on the column blocks the index.** A plain index on `users.email` can't be used when the column is wrapped in `lower()`. The database scans all of `users` and lowercases every email. That would take longer as the table grows.\n- **`orders.user_id` may have no index.** If it doesn't, the join also scans `orders`.\n- **`SELECT *` pulls every column from both tables.** That adds I/O and network cost, and wide columns make it worse. It also returns `id` and other column names twice, which can break row mapping in the app.\n\n**Fixes, in order of impact**\n1. Add an expression index that matches the query:\n   ```sql\n   CREATE INDEX CONCURRENTLY idx_users_email_lower ON users (lower(email));\n   ```\n   This is Postgres syntax. Other databases have equivalents, such as a functional index in MySQL 8 or a computed column in SQL Server.\n   Or normalize emails to lowercase on write and drop the `lower()`. If your Postgres has `citext`, that works too.\n2. Make sure `orders(user_id)` is indexed:\n   ```sql\n   CREATE INDEX CONCURRENTLY idx_orders_user_id ON orders (user_id);\n   ```\n3. Select only the columns the page renders.\n\n**Why it got slow last week**\nThe query itself looks like it has always been written this way, so something else probably changed. Check these:\n- A dropped or rebuilt index, or a migration that changed the `email` column type or collation.\n- A jump in table size, or stale statistics (try `ANALYZE users, orders`).\n- A recent deploy that added the `lower()`. `git log -p -- query.sql` and your app's deploy history would show that.\n\nTo confirm, run `EXPLAIN (ANALYZE, BUFFERS)` on the query. If you see `Seq Scan on users` with a filter on `lower(email)`, that's the problem.\n\nI can't see your schema, so I'm guessing about the existing indexes. If you paste the `\\d users` and `\\d orders` output or the EXPLAIN plan, I can be more specific. I can also check `app.log` or `access.log` here for slow-request timing around when it regressed.", "commits": [], "branch": "main", "before": {}, "after": {}}}